/* Planning-build-only overlay, applied by tools/partition_layout.py
 * alongside a board's layout glue when planning (never in real builds).
 *
 * Some upstream board dts point /chosen/zephyr,code-partition at a partition
 * label the fork's layout deletes (e.g. nrf54h20dk's cpuapp_slot0_partition).
 * Real builds don't notice: the bootloader image re-points the property via
 * boot/zephyr/app.overlay (boot_partition) and application images via their
 * board overlay (the fork's slot0). The planning build (hello_world) has
 * neither, so the dangling reference fails devicetree compilation. Deleting
 * the property here is safe for planning: plan_partitions() and
 * plan_code_partition_split() derive everything from the flash devices, not
 * from chosen.
 */
/ {
	chosen {
		/delete-property/ zephyr,code-partition;
	};
};